Log ENOTCONN from shutdown() as a warning in trantor

When the peer has already disconnected, Socket::closeWrite() gets
ENOTCONN from shutdown(). That is expected and harmless, so this patch
logs it as a warning instead of as a system error (RONDB-1033).

diff --git a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/trantor-1.5.29/trantor/net/inner/Socket.cc b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/trantor-1.5.29/trantor/net/inner/Socket.cc
index 2aff5a03953..bbb1a4a2b4e 100644
--- a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/trantor-1.5.29/trantor/net/inner/Socket.cc
+++ b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/trantor-1.5.29/trantor/net/inner/Socket.cc
@@ -107,7 +107,14 @@ void Socket::closeWrite()
     if (::shutdown(sockFd_, SD_SEND) < 0)
 #endif
     {
-        LOG_SYSERR << "sockets::shutdownWrite";
+        if (errno == ENOTCONN)
+        {
+            LOG_WARN << "sockets::shutdownWrite - peer already disconnected";
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            LOG_SYSERR << "sockets::shutdownWrite";
+        }
     }
 }
 int Socket::read(char *buffer, uint64_t len)
